 Prefer Settings → Keyboard for editing shortcuts interactively.
 
+### Chat card disclosure config
+
+`ui.disclosure` controls whether transcript cards start open or collapsed, independently for five part types: `thinking`, `skillInvocation`, `toolResult`, `toolDetails` (the tool execution details body), and `toolDiff` (the tool execution diff body). Each accepts one of four modes:
+
+- `none`: closed. This is the default for every part except `toolDiff`.
+- `live`: open while the session is active, closed once work finishes.
+- `last`: open only for the most recently rendered transcript entry.
+- `all`: always open. This is the default for `toolDiff`.
+
+An empty or missing `ui.disclosure` reproduces the pre-existing UI behavior exactly. Error cards stay open regardless of mode: `toolResult` when the result is an error, and `toolDetails` when the tool execution status is `error`. A user can still collapse any card by clicking it in any mode.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ui": {
+    "disclosure": {
+      "thinking": "all",
+      "toolDetails": "all",
+      "toolDiff": "all"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
